schema_id: atlas.structured-tool-input
schema_version: 1
schema_kind: workflow_tool_input
status: ACTIVE

description: >
  Ordered structured arguments for deterministic Parent Atlas DAG/tool execution.
  Inputs use AtlasStructuredValueV1 instead of an opaque JSON object so positional
  order, named arguments, duplicate/source object entries, 64-bit integers,
  references and structural provenance survive TypeScript/protobuf/Go/Python
  transport. The target tool schema remains authoritative for semantic validation.

fields:
  schema: { type: literal, value: atlas.structured-tool-input.v1 }
  requestId: { type: string, required: true }
  workflowId: { type: string, required: true }
  actionId: { type: string, required: true }
  dagNodeId: { type: string, required: true }
  capability: { type: string, required: true }
  toolSchemaRevision: { type: string, required: true }
  arguments:
    type: array
    default: []
    items:
      type: object
      fields:
        ordinal: { type: integer, minimum: 0 }
        name: { type: string, nullable: true }
        role:
          type: enum
          values: [POSITIONAL, NAMED, VAR_POSITIONAL, VAR_KEYWORD, OPTIONS, PAYLOAD, REFERENCE]
        value: { type: atlas.structured-value.v1, required: true }
  evidenceRefs: { type: string_array, default: [] }
  exactPromotionRefs: { type: string_array, default: [] }
  producerRevision: { type: string, required: true }
  checksum: { type: string, required: true }

invariants:
  - arguments preserve ordinal order and MUST NOT be represented as a map when positional/source ordering matters
  - a name does not replace ordinal; named arguments remain ordered observations for deterministic replay
  - nested OBJECT/MAP values preserve repeated ordered entries through AtlasStructuredValueV1
  - tool execution MUST validate these values against the capability's revisioned input schema before dispatch
  - SYMBOL_REF/PACKET_REF/TENSOR_REF/SOURCE_REF values are hydrated/authorized by their canonical owners; a tool input may not reinterpret backend IDs as canonical refs
  - exactPromotionRefs/evidenceRefs constrain execution and are not inferred from serialized argument bytes
  - the structured tool input is replayable but does not itself authorize side effects; existing workflow/action authorization remains authoritative
